Report #169, clarified by the user: triple the FACTION-ALIGNED BATTLE NPCs
of Wintergrasp (the keep/outside armies that fight the battle), NOT the
PvE wildlife -- the earlier rev_wg_npc_respawn_30s.sql migration targets
wildlife and was the wrong interpretation; that fix stands for what it
covers, and this core change covers the armies.

The armies are spawned in code, not the DB: OnBattleStart walks the
WGKeepNPC (45 rows) and WGOutsideNPC (14 rows) tables and calls
SpawnCreature once per row per faction. Army size is therefore a code
constant, not a spawn count -- no DB migration can triple it.

Change: each table row now spawns WG_ARMY_COPIES_PER_ROW (3) copies in a
small ring (offsets {0,0}, {3,2}, {-3,-2} yards) instead of one, tripling
both armies: 135 keep guards + 42 outside guards per side, all still
tracked in KeepCreature/OutsideCreature so the existing hide/show,
faction-swap and cleanup logic works unchanged. New constants in
BattlefieldWG.h next to the other WG counts.

Touches: src/server/game/Battlefield/Zones/BattlefieldWG.{h,cpp}
